erClient.get` in `weather.py` now retries when the server returns 503. It makes 3 attempts in total, waiting 0.5s, then 1s between them (each wait doubles).\n\n- **Only 503 is retried.** Any other HTTP error, and network errors like timeouts, still raise straight away, as before.\n- **After the 3rd 503,** the original `HTTPError` is raised so callers see the same exception as before.\n- **New optional settings:** `max_attempts` (default 3) and `backoff` (starting delay, default 0.5s) on `__init__`. Existing calls don't need to change.\n\nI tested it against a real local HTTP server with backoff turned down to 0.05s:\n\n| Server responses | Result |\n|---|---|\n| 503, 503, 200 | returned the data on the 3rd attempt |\n| 503 every time | 3 attempts, then `HTTPError 503` |\n| 500 | 1 attempt, then `HTTPError 500` (no retry) |\n| 200 | returned the data on the 1st attempt |\n\nThe repo has no test suite, so I didn't add one. The test above was run once and not saved.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 5, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 70460, "requests_cache_write": 108789, "requests_cost_usd": 0.593665, "requests_count": 5, "requests_input_uncached": 12, "requests_output": 1779, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial4", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 66, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:38:56.089458+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 23.322, "t_checker_s": 1.928, "t_env_setup_s": 0.0, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1791, "tok